        <div id="celiac-math" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. Celiac Protein Powder: How Much Gluten Is Too Much?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Parts per million sounds abstract, so it helps to do the arithmetic. A product at the FDA limit of 20 ppm contains 20 mg of gluten per kilogram. A typical 30 g scoop is 0.03 kg, so even a powder sitting right at the limit delivers about 0.6 mg of gluten per scoop. A GFCO-certified powder at 10 ppm delivers 0.3 mg or less, and most tested products land well below their limit.
          </p>

          <p>
            Research on gluten thresholds in celiac disease has generally found that most people tolerate less than about 10 mg of gluten a day without measurable intestinal damage, while regular intake of around 50 mg a day caused damage in a well-known controlled trial. Tolerance varies, and some people with celiac disease react to less, but those figures are the basis for the 20 ppm standard. By that measure, even two scoops of a powder at the FDA limit add only a small fraction of the daily threshold.
          </p>

          <p>
            The practical risk, then, is not a gluten-free-labeled powder sitting at 18 ppm. It is a product that is mislabeled, a flavor that contains a gluten ingredient you missed, or a product with no claim at all that turns out to be badly contaminated. Certification protects against the first, careful label reading against the second, and simply avoiding no-claim products against the third.
          </p>

          <p>
            That is also why the number of servings matters a little. Someone drinking three shakes a day, eating gluten-free bread and pasta, and using gluten-free baking flours is stacking many small exposures. Choosing certified products for the foods you eat most often is a sensible way to keep the daily total low.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">By the Numbers</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
