          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Most protein powders are gluten-free by nature, so the question is not whether you can find one but how much verification you need. For celiac disease, choose a third-party certified powder such as Garden of Life Sport or Ascent 100% Whey when you can. For general gluten avoidance, a labeled gluten-free isolate with a short ingredient list, such as Isopure Zero Carb or Dymatize ISO100, is a sound choice.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, check the exact flavor for oats, malt and baked pieces, confirm the seal on the tub, and get tested for celiac disease before cutting out gluten if you have not already.
